<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaki Sherocho</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaki Sherocho was the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feodosia">Kaffa</a>, in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. He resisted the armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a> until 1897, when Kaffa was conquered and he was captured and taken north. The kingdom was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>, and he died in captivity years later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaki-sherocho.jpg" alt="Gaki Sherocho" width="320" height="346" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paul Buffet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gaki_Sherocho_in_ceremonial_dress.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
